1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,827
Imagine you're paying online, and the moment you tap Pay, an SMS arrives on your phone.

2
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,765
It has a 6-digit code that's valid for only a few minutes.

3
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:14,777
When you tap Pay or Login, the server creates a random number.

4
00:00:16,567 --> 00:00:19,720
The server sends the OTP message to an SMS gateway.

5
00:00:20,067 --> 00:00:23,458
The SMS gateway passes this message to your telecom operator's network.

6
00:00:24,633 --> 00:00:26,631
The server checks whether the OTP is correct.

7
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:31,196
It also checks that the OTP hasn't expired and hasn't been used before.

8
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:36,202
Remember, a bank never asks for your OTP by call, or by message.

9
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:40,162
Never share your OTP with anyone, whoever they may be.

10
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:45,280
To understand the whole process, watch the full video. Thank you!

